WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:09.960
At the foot of Lothric Castle, an old path still runs below the tower in the Undead Settlement.

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:16.500
It was used to transport sacrifices to the Cathedral of the Deep.

00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:19.680
You should see where it leads....

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:23.760
if you've the stones for it

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:28.220
*Breathy Cackle*

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:33.440
So, we're travelling along the Road of Sacrifices toward the Cathedral of the Deep

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:37.980
and Aldrich, Saint of the Deep, apparently lies within.

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:39.960
Aldrich is a Lord of Cinder

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:43.580
And a Lord of Cinder is someone who has linked the fire

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:44.440
in a previous age.

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:47.340
The were so mighty and powerful that they could link

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:50.200
the fire and extend the age of flame.

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:54.160
But that was in a past age and now alongside

00:00:54.160 --> 00:00:57.720
the other Lords of Cinder, Aldrich has been resurrected

00:00:57.720 --> 00:00:59.840
to link the fire once more, but this time

00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:02.900
he's hiding from his duty, he's run away

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:06.180
to his home, at the base of Lothric Castle.

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:09.540
The Crestfallen Knight speaks of sacrifices

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:12.260
that were presumably going to Aldrich

00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:15.440
because Aldrich is referenced as a devourer of men.

00:01:15.980 --> 00:01:19.620
So this path to Aldrich, this Road of Sacrifices,

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:22.020
I think it was used a long time ago.

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:25.340
Because this path is now crawling with Corvian

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:28.160
creatures, who were these deformed beast-men

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:30.860
who we learn more about from their weapons.

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:32.740
And they have a fascinating little story.

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:37.320
The Storyteller's Staff reveals that the casters are

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:40.480
heretical storytellers who share tales of the

00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:43.920
Painted World to forlorn souls, however the

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:46.920
tellers themselves, they're also wretched beings

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:48.660
with no place to go.

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:51.920
The Corvians with the great knife are named as

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:55.680
unwanted. They're guided by the storytellers and

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:58.960
they wield this big old knife that is used to intimidate

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:02.360
foes, but all it does reveal how afraid they are

00:02:02.360 --> 00:02:05.860
themselves. Because they fight like animals backed

00:02:05.860 --> 00:02:06.860
into a corner.

00:02:09.820 --> 00:02:13.180
Some wield great Corvian Scythes, which directly

00:02:13.180 --> 00:02:16.020
reference Priscilla of the Painted World.

00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:18.940
And there are so many similarities between these

00:02:18.940 --> 00:02:21.400
creatures and Priscilla. Uhh, if you remember Priscilla

00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:25.660
was a crossbreed between a dragon and most likely

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:28.720
a Lord, or a God. She was locked away in a painting

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:31.780
Where she speaks affectionately of all the other

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:34.200
unwanted beings that were locked away with her.

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:37.580
"Priscilla speaks" This land is peaceful.. its inhabitants kind.

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:40.720
"Vaati begins narration again" So by mimicking Priscilla's

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:43.960
weaponry, and by telling us stories it's really clear

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:46.820
that these creatures admire, or maybe even worship her.

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:51.400
Because these are unwanted, lost creatures, and Priscilla

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:56.040
is the champion of the deformed, and the unwanted, and the rejected.

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:01.920
If you drop off the bridge here you'll find this hidden

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:06.480
little alcove, this cavethat  hides Morne's ring and a Divine

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:10.120
Braille tome. And in Episode 3 we actually rescued the

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:12.220
two characters that these items are associated with.

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:17.060
Uhhh, Eygon of Carim, and his captive Irina.

00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:20.340
So considering how close this little cave is and the items

00:03:20.540 --> 00:03:24.220
within it I really imagine these two sitting here, resting

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:28.060
on their journey to their next destination. Eygon is

00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:30.680
a knight of Carim and Morne's Ring is a ring that's

00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:34.420
given to knights of Carim to boost miracles.

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:36.740
The character named Morne we haven't met yet, and we

00:03:36.740 --> 00:03:39.760
might never meet him. He's described to be this

00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:42.740
high-ranking apostle within Carim's church system

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:46.600
and he laboured with the Goddess Caitha to provide

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:50.140
comfort to the suffering. Caitha has been referenced

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:52.800
before. She's really frequently mentioned in Dark Souls

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:56.600
II descriptions as this goddess of tears, who's

00:03:56.700 --> 00:03:59.660
known as a compassionate being that's with us

00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:02.460
in times of tragedy. Although, there's some item

00:04:02.540 --> 00:04:05.480
descriptions that say that she's a demoness, that guides

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:07.200
us toward misfortune.

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:11.000
And finally, we clear the Road of Sacrifices and

00:04:11.220 --> 00:04:14.620
below us is the Crucifixion Woods, but before that

00:04:14.920 --> 00:04:18.700
we come across a unkindled traveller who is coming

00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:21.500
through here in a much the same way we are.

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:23.460
, and that's something I missed in Bloodborne.

00:04:23.460 --> 00:04:25.740
Dark Souls is very much about meeting characters

00:04:25.980 --> 00:04:29.100
who really inhabit the same world you do and

00:04:29.140 --> 00:04:30.920
empathize with the same struggles.

00:04:52.380 --> 00:04:54.320
Anri's Narration Continues

00:04:54.320 --> 00:04:57.020
Beyond the flooded woods lies Farron Keep

00:04:57.160 --> 00:05:01.040
home of the Undead Legion. Further yet is the Cathedral of the Deep.

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:20.420
Vaati Continues

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:24.260
So Anri of Astora is female here, right? But if you play as

00:05:24.460 --> 00:05:26.940
a female character then she'll be a man.

00:05:31.160 --> 00:05:34.640
You'll understand why this is in a later episode, I

00:05:34.640 --> 00:05:37.720
promise. And I can't wait until April 12th, when everyone

00:05:37.780 --> 00:05:40.960
has this game, and when I can invade you guys.

00:05:41.060 --> 00:05:44.220
As of this date only press and streamers have access to

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:47.640
the english PC version, and, while the current early

00:05:47.840 --> 00:05:51.040
access system is this complete mess, it's completely

00:05:51.100 --> 00:05:54.140
screwed up that the game is out early like this.

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:57.880
I just can't help but cover it early, I'm sorry.

00:05:57.880 --> 00:06:00.360
Making videos is half the fun for me, I can't resist.

00:06:00.720 --> 00:06:03.560
One good thing did come out of it, though. I was the first

00:06:03.580 --> 00:06:07.680
to kill PvP streamer Peeve Peeverson, so that was fun

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:10.140
I mean it was fun for me, I don't know if it was fun for

00:06:10.240 --> 00:06:13.300
him. But, uh, he gets me back for it later, so it's okay.

00:06:14.660 --> 00:06:18.680
Back at the shrine we meet Sirris, of the Sunless Realms.

00:06:42.120 --> 00:06:45.460
She certainly fits the bill as a blade of the Dark Moon

00:06:45.520 --> 00:06:49.060
and the Sunless Realms could well be a reference to

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:52.500
Anor Londo and the illusion of sunlight that Gwyndolin

00:06:52.660 --> 00:06:57.140
projected upon it, all that time ago. But that remains to be seen

00:06:57.340 --> 00:07:00.280
and remains to be confirmed. Back in the woods

00:07:00.460 --> 00:07:03.040
we take out the giant enemy crab, that you'll have to

00:07:03.080 --> 00:07:06.000
take out fairly quickly, otherwise it can actually bury

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:08.560
back beneath the ground and come up again with

00:07:08.700 --> 00:07:11.980
full health. One of them drops the Great Swamp Ring

00:07:11.980 --> 00:07:15.280
which boosts pyromancy and reminds us that pyromancy

00:07:15.280 --> 00:07:18.380
is supposedly born of the Chaos Flame.

00:07:18.380 --> 00:07:21.300
Nearby is the conjurer set and a tome that teaches us

00:07:21.320 --> 00:07:24.540
ancient pyromancies. So let's have a talk about

00:07:24.660 --> 00:07:27.720
pyromancy. If you're rusty on your Dark Souls lore

00:07:27.860 --> 00:07:31.260
remember that the Chaos Flame was created long ago

00:07:31.380 --> 00:07:35.200
by the witch of Izaloth. The Witch tried to create a flame

00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:38.420
that could replace the fading first flame, so that the light

00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:41.280
of the world could be restored, but everything went

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:45.080
wrong. And, instead, the flame consumed her and

00:07:45.300 --> 00:07:49.100
spiraled out of control and created demons. One of the

00:07:49.260 --> 00:07:52.940
witch's sisters escaped and became the mother of

00:07:52.980 --> 00:07:57.380
pyromancy. Her name was Quelana, and her art was

00:07:57.500 --> 00:08:00.540
borne of the Chaos Flame. She taught apprentices

00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:04.320
, the art was passed down, and as a result the further

00:08:04.440 --> 00:08:08.280
back you go with pyromancy, the closer you get to the

00:08:08.340 --> 00:08:12.520
more powerful, the more primal spells. Cornyx, a

00:08:12.520 --> 00:08:16.280
pyromancer we met in the Undead Settlement tells us

00:08:16.360 --> 00:08:17.120
of this.

00:08:32.500 --> 00:08:33.860
Cornyx's Narration Continues

00:08:33.860 --> 00:08:37.520
At least, that is what pyromancers of the Great Swamp

00:08:37.740 --> 00:08:38.700
believe.

00:08:40.020 --> 00:08:42.380
The place is called Izalith.

00:08:56.540 --> 00:08:57.420
Vaati Continues

00:08:57.420 --> 00:09:00.540
He says that the lands of the Lords converge upon

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:04.140
Lothric, and that Izalith drifts comparatively close as

00:09:04.200 --> 00:09:08.420
well. So just like characters and souls are reborn and

00:09:08.420 --> 00:09:12.120
we see them again, just as time is convoluted, and people

00:09:12.240 --> 00:09:16.140
are shifting in and out. Are powerful places somehow drawn

00:09:16.340 --> 00:09:19.520
closer to the land of the Lords when the flame fades

00:09:19.640 --> 00:09:22.580
as well? Could this explain what Emma said about the

00:09:22.740 --> 00:09:24.120
Lords of Cinder?

00:09:34.740 --> 00:09:37.900
Within the central ruins of The Crucifixion Woods is a

00:09:37.960 --> 00:09:39.840
familiar figure.

00:09:44.040 --> 00:09:47.080
This Crystal Sage is one of two sages that went on to

00:09:47.080 --> 00:09:49.180
ally with the Undead Legion.

00:09:49.720 --> 00:09:53.060
He did so to train the Sorcerers of Farron, which

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:55.480
explains the multitude of undead sorcerers we

00:09:55.480 --> 00:09:57.260
we just fought our way through.

00:09:57.260 --> 00:10:00.420
These Sorcerers of Farron's Abyss Watchers were

00:10:00.420 --> 00:10:03.280
known to be lonesome warriors who would only

00:10:03.540 --> 00:10:07.240
rely upon more pragmatic spells.

00:10:09.340 --> 00:10:12.840
Phase two of the Sage is ridiculous. That was probably

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:16.040
the boss that I had the most trouble with on my first

00:10:16.040 --> 00:10:17.780
play through. I must have attempted it like five times,

00:10:17.860 --> 00:10:21.200
because all of these illusions shoot so many spells.

00:10:21.200 --> 00:10:24.620
And it's difficult to dodge them and not get stun-locked

00:10:24.740 --> 00:10:28.940
So my advice for this 1. Do a lot of strafing and sprinting.

00:10:29.100 --> 00:10:32.540
And if you have a heavy weapon, just switch it out to a

00:10:32.640 --> 00:10:35.280
fist and smack one of the illusions and move on to the

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:38.860
next one. And the when you get to the real boss,

00:10:38.860 --> 00:10:40.220
just smack him into the ground.

00:10:42.040 --> 00:10:45.600
A sorcerer with his sanity does remain within the Ruined

00:10:45.600 --> 00:10:46.800
Keep.

00:12:05.020 --> 00:12:07.980
Around him are hundreds of valuable scrolls.

00:12:08.340 --> 00:12:10.720
The hard work of an entire lifetime.

00:12:11.980 --> 00:12:13.700
Sorry! I had to do that.

00:12:14.300 --> 00:12:17.660
As we return to the Firelink Shrine, Yuria tells us about

00:12:17.700 --> 00:12:20.380
her growing concern with Orbeck.

00:13:34.900 --> 00:13:37.840
Let me know if you liked this episode. This one was

00:13:37.900 --> 00:13:40.740
much more focused on the lore, but I could also focus

00:13:40.760 --> 00:13:44.260
more on tips, or items, or little tricks that I've learned on

00:13:44.380 --> 00:13:47.240
my first play through. So, let me know, and I'll see you

00:13:47.240 --> 00:13:48.300
next time.

